: "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.3175, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026003942/meta-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0043", "ticker": "META", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.2735, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026003942/meta-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0089", "ticker": "META", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.0518, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000162828026003942/meta-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "META_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0032", "ticker": "META", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 0.8044, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000132680125000017/meta-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "META_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0031", "ticker": "META", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 0.7815, "filing_name": "Meta Platforms Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326801/000132680125000017/meta-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 115, "dropped_candidates": 203, "token_estimate": 31891, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Both companies describe advertising as the core revenue exposure, but they frame the risk differently. Alphabet's fiscal 2025 10-K (ended December 31, 2025) says it generated more than 70% of total revenues from online advertising and warns that reduced advertiser spending, loss of partners, shifts in online advertising and ad-blocking technologies could harm its business [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000]. It also says adverse macroeconomic conditions have affected, and may affect, advertising demand [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001]. Meta's fiscal 2025 10-K (ended December 31, 2025) stresses that the substantial majority of its revenue comes from advertising on mobile devices and that changes by Apple, Google and other platform providers have limited its ad targeting and measurement [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015]. Meta also lists user engagement declines, ad pricing and marketer demand, product shifts toward lower-monetizing formats such as Reels, and regulatory developments as factors that can hurt ad revenue [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0009]. The filings do not rank these risks, and Keel does not give investment advice.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "GOOG", "company": "Alphabet Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Alphabet generated more than 70% of total revenues from online advertising in fiscal 2025 (ended December 31, 2025), and says reduced advertiser spending, loss of partners, or ad-blocking and anti-personalization technologies could harm its business.", "citations": ["GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Alphabet says AI is quickly reshaping the advertising industry and there is no assurance it will adapt effectively with new ad formats; advertiser spending also tends to correlate with economic conditions.", "citations": ["GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000", "GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The online advertising share of revenue was stated as more than 75% in fiscal 2024 (ended December 31, 2024) and fiscal 2023 (ended December 31, 2023), and more than 80% in fiscal 2022 (ended December 31, 2022).", "citations": ["GOOG_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0000", "GOOG_10K_2023-12-31__risk_factors__0000", "GOOG_10K_2022-12-31__risk_factors__0000"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "META", "company": "Meta Platforms Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Meta's 10-K for fiscal 2025 (ended December 31, 2025) lists factors that can hurt advertising revenue, including lower user engagement, marketer demand and ad pricing, and third-party policy changes by Apple and Google that limit ad delivery, targeting or measurement.", "citations": ["META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0009"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Meta says its advertising revenue has been negatively impacted by iOS changes beginning in 2021, and that the substantial majority of its revenue comes from advertising on mobile devices it does not control.", "citations": ["META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Meta expects Reels to monetize at a lower rate than Feed and Stories, and cites government actions that could impair its ability to sell or deliver advertising, including China-based reseller revenue.", "citations": ["META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0023", "META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0069"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Theme", "Alphabet (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025)", "Meta (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025)"], "rows": [["Revenue concentration", "More than 70% of total revenues from online advertising [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0000]", "Substantial majority of revenue from mobile advertising [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015]"], ["Targeting and measurement", "Technologies make personalized ads harder or block ads [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001]", "Apple and Google platform changes limit targeting and measurement [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0016]"], ["Economic sensitivity", "Advertiser spending correlates with economic conditions [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001]", "Spending fluctuates w